  </widget>
  <widget class="QLabel" name="lblGroupsStatus">
   <property name="geometry">
    <rect>
     <x>210</x>
     <y>150</y>
     <width>390</width>
     <height>25</height>
    </rect>
   </property>
   <property name="text">
    <string>Auto (faults detected)</string>
   </property>
  </widget>
  <!-- Rotation alignment checkbox -->
  <widget class="QCheckBox" name="rotate_checkbox">
   <property name="geometry">
    <rect>
     <x>20</x>
     <y>185</y>
     <width>580</width>
     <height>21</height>
    </rect>
   </property>
   <property name="text">
    <string>Align model with axes (rotate so sides best match X / Y)</string>
   </property>
   <property name="toolTip">
    <string>When checked, compute the best-fit rotation so the model sides align with the X and Y axes, rotate the X/Y columns of the geology and orientation CSVs in place on disk, and save the rotation matrix to rotation_matrix.csv in the output folder.</string>
   </property>
  </widget>
  <!-- Translate-to-origin checkbox -->
  <widget class="QCheckBox" name="translate_origin_checkbox">
   <property name="geometry">
    <rect>
     <x>20</x>
     <y>212</y>
     <width>580</width>
     <height>21</height>
    </rect>
   </property>
   <property name="text">
    <string>Translate to origin (DTM corner closest to (0,0) becomes the new origin)</string>
   </property>
   <property name="toolTip">
    <string>When checked, derive the rotation angle from the longest side of the source DTM and use the DTM bounding-box corner closest to the CRS origin as the rotation pivot, then translate everything so that pivot lands at (0, 0). Geology and orientation CSVs, the AOI polygon, and the resampled topography are all transformed consistently. The applied transform (rotation + translation) is recorded in rotation_matrix.csv. Implies axis alignment — overrides the "Align model with axes" pivot logic when checked.</string>
   </property>
  </widget>
